# Dissection Practice: Bot2 answers the spell with Dawn's Truce, so Bot2 (the player) has hexproof until end of turn and is no longer a
# legal target (CR 608.2b, 702.11b). Bot2's life total is not frozen, only the targeting changed. The spell does not fizzle: the
# Misshapen Fiend is still a legal target, so it resolves and performs every instruction that does not affect an illegal target (CR
# 608.2b): Bot2 is not affected, so loses nothing, but "you gain 1 life" is its own instruction that does not affect the opponent
# (no "that much"), so Bot1 still gains 1 (21) and the Fiend still gets +1/+1 (2/2). Control: the first Dissection Practice scenario.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Misshapen Fiend
Swamp x4
Dissection Practice
Swamp x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Dawn's Truce
Plains x5
Plains x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Hand.Misshapen Fiend.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dissection Practice.Cast
Bot1.Target(Bot2)
Bot1.Target(Misshapen Fiend)
Bot1.Target()
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot2.Hand.Dawn's Truce.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Life = 21
Bot1.Battlefield.Misshapen Fiend.Power = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Misshapen Fiend.Toughness = 2
Bot1.Graveyard = Dissection Practice; Black Lotus
